       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** At this level the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't offset that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
